cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use RangeSieve in research, cite the software version you used and the statistical methods you applied.'
type: software
title: 'RangeSieve: numerical data exploration and outlier review'
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-21'
doi: '10.5281/zenodo.23540904'
authors:
  - given-names: 'Annina R.'
    family-names: 'Meyer'
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3110-6598'
    website: 'https://github.com/anninameyer'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/anninameyer/RangeSieve'
url: 'https://github.com/anninameyer/RangeSieve'
license: MIT
abstract: 'Browser-based numerical data exploration, outlier screening, plausibility assessment, sensitivity analysis, and local scientific exports. Research data stays in the user’s browser: all analyses run locally, with no research data uploaded or stored by RangeSieve. The online and self-contained offline editions share the same source.'
keywords:
  - scientific software
  - exploratory data analysis
  - outlier screening
  - reproducible research
  - privacy
